Since you want the real enterprise-grade pattern, I’ll show you the Advanced Angular Permission + Policy Engine architecture.
This is used in large SaaS dashboards (100–500 screens) and scales much better than simple permission checks.

1. Problem with Normal Permission System

Typical Angular approach:

permission.has('DELETE_USER')

Problems in large systems:

❌ Thousands of permission checks everywhere
❌ Hardcoded logic in components
❌ Feature flags impossible
❌ Tenant rules difficult
❌ A/B testing difficult
❌ Dynamic UI impossible

So large systems move to a Policy Engine.

2. Enterprise Access Model

Large systems combine 4 models.

RBAC  → Role Based Access Control
ABAC  → Attribute Based Access Control
PBAC  → Policy Based Access Control
FF    → Feature Flags

Example rule:

ALLOW delete_user

IF
role = ADMIN
AND tenant = EU
AND feature_flag = USER_DELETE_ENABLED

Angular only asks policy engine.

